{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462553-low-harmony","id":462553,"title":"Low Harmony","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-30T12:08:48-07:00","id":462553,"title":"Low Harmony","content":"Hi, just looking for some clarification on Low Harmony situations. There's a little overlap between narrative discussion and mechanics, which makes it a little hard to suss out what's happening. Relevant content is on page 96 of WW 2e.<br /> <br /> Let's see if I've got this right:<br /> **************<br /> Low Harmony Uratha must change form once per scence. They can avoid this change by spending Essence and/or actions, as per the small list also on page 96. This change however cannot be avoided if the uratha is stressed, for example, combat. In this case, an uratha shifts &quot;one form toward an appropriate form each turn.&quot; I assume that the forms are on a little line.<br /> <br /> <b>Coward</b> Urhan - Urhsul - Hishu - Dalu - Gauru - <b>FIGHTAN</b><br /> <br /> If you're lucky and enter combat in Urhan without the desire to run away, you have 4 turns before you hit Gauru and 3 or more before you Kuruth. If you're in Hishu, 2 turns. And so forth. Again, this <i>cannot</i> be avoided by spending Essence or Willpower and there is no roll to resist.<br /> ***************<br /> <br /> This effectively means that upon hitting Harmony 3, you're on a timer to kuruth every time you want to fight anything.... or does it? Can you change tactics in the middle of combat to <i>run away</i> or <i>harassment tactics!</i> and start shifting toward urhan again?<br /> <br /> I'm really feeling like the Low Harmony mechanics are not meshing at all with the way WWs are presented as clever careful hunters. Especially with tribes like Hunters In Darkness who are all about traps. Or Iron Masters who blend in so well with the humans. It feels like instead of being a spirit-focused being caught up in the hunt, you're abandoning your tactics for extreme unreliability in the face of anything stressful.<br /> <br /> It also feels really DM-fiat heavy. My Elodoth is talking to <i>Important Bad Guy. </i>About something <i>Important. </i>Is that stressful enough to force changes? In this case, hishu is probably best. Does that mesh with this? Do I have to convince my DM everytime stress pops up that I'm already in the best form for the job?<br /> <br /> It feels all wishy washy and unclear!! Blearragghhhh.................<br /> <br /> Okay done.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T12:28:44-07:00","id":462603,"title":"","content":"It's kinda hard to be a &quot;clever, careful hunter&quot; when you're riddled with spiritual maladies. Nobody said a werewolf had to be an efficient hunter. Merely that he has to hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T12:48:14-07:00","id":462613,"title":"","content":"At Low Harmony you're eschewing the clever and careful bit and just becoming more of a predator like spirits are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T12:59:44-07:00","id":462621,"title":"","content":"I would argue that there's not a neat little line, but rather that Dalu and Urshul are always the middle forms. If you're in Urhan and you need to fight, you'll go to Urshul before you need to go Gauru. If you're in Hishu and need to run, you'll go Dalu before Urhan. And that's if you want to take your time getting to the form you need that you're not at.<br /> <br /> As to the Elodoth example, Hishu seems like the right form for that up to the point where knives come out, so yeah, no arguement needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T13:08:38-07:00","id":462626,"title":"","content":"Urshul is probably the second best form to fight in after gauru, so I certainly wouldn't put that behind Hishu in the &quot;appropriate for combat&quot; scale at any rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T13:53:58-07:00","id":462649,"title":"","content":"You automatically assume the form best suited to the task you pick in a stressful situation. Want to run? Urhan. Hide? Hishu. Push around? Dalu. Chase? Urshal. Fight? Garou.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter what form you are wearing at the time, it matters what you want to do when the stress kicks in. Your spiritual side automatically assumes the best suited form for the task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T12:28:41-07:00","id":463725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Full Time GM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462553-low-harmony?p=462649#post462649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You automatically assume the form best suited to the task you pick in a stressful situation. Want to run? Urhan. Hide? Hishu. Push around? Dalu. Chase? Urshal. Fight? Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would change Fight to Kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T13:03:23-07:00","id":463761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Full Time GM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462553-low-harmony?p=462649#post462649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You automatically assume the form best suited to the task you pick in a stressful situation. Want to run? Urhan. Hide? Hishu. Push around? Dalu. Chase? Urshal. Fight? Garou.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter what form you are wearing at the time, it matters what you want to do when the stress kicks in. Your spiritual side automatically assumes the best suited form for the task.</div> </div> </div> </div>It kind of does though, because it says you shift <i>one form towards</i> the most appropriate form for the task each turn. Its not entirely clear what constitutes shifting towards a form. I would assume Hishu and Urhan are the farthest ends of the spectrum with Gauru in the middle separated by Dalu or Urshul on either side. But that's not exactly spelled out, and it's not clear if it's entirely linear or if it loops around.<br /> <br /> So my assumption would be that if you begin combat in Hishu and your instinct is to run, you'll shift to Dalu on your first turn, Gauru on your second, Urshul on your third, and finally end in Urhan on your fourth turn. (Unless they do in fact loop around, in which case you'd go straight to Urhan.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T13:19:15-07:00","id":463781,"title":"","content":"That does sound like what they intended, but that raises other complications. Say you've already used gauru this scene and need to run. Do you get stuck at dalu? Does it skip gauru and go straight to urshul? Does entering gauru a second time make you fall into kuruth?<br /> <br /> It almost seems like whoever wrote that bit was playing Werewolf the Apocalypse just before and got their wires crossed, because it would work fine there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T13:53:16-07:00","id":463845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462553-low-harmony?p=463781#post463781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does sound like what they intended, but that raises other complications. Say you've already used gauru this scene and need to run. Do you get stuck at dalu? Does it skip gauru and go straight to urshul? Does entering gauru a second time make you fall into kuruth?<br /> <br /> It almost seems like whoever wrote that bit was playing Werewolf the Apocalypse just before and got their wires crossed, because it would work fine there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess allowing it to loop around would solve that problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:21:26-07:00","id":463870,"title":"","content":"I just assumed that yopu skipped garou if the situation didn't call for fighting. So if you were in hishu and wanted to run, you would be forced into dalu, then urshul, then urban.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:38:18-07:00","id":463890,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure this would actually work at all considering at the level we're talking you can reflexively shift voluntarily to whatever form you want. So if you're in hishu and you're instincts want to run but you don't then you'd shift to dalu... and then shift right back into hishu the next chance you got. And if you did want to run you'd just shift straight to urhan and get straight outta dodge. <br /> <br /> So I'd just ignore that bit entirely and have them shift straight into whatever form their instincts thought they needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:50:44-07:00","id":463904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462553-low-harmony?p=463890#post463890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure this would actually work at all considering at the level we're talking you can reflexively shift voluntarily to whatever form you want. So if you're in hishu and you're instincts want to run but you don't then you'd shift to dalu... and then shift right back into hishu the next chance you got. And if you did want to run you'd just shift straight to urhan and get straight outta dodge.<br /> <br /> So I'd just ignore that bit entirely and have them shift straight into whatever form their instincts thought they needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea is supposed to be that if you didn't want to run, Urhan wouldn't be the form you were shifting towards. It reads to me less as something that might cause you to take a form you don't want, and more as a speed bump to reaching the form you do want. So yeah, if you were stressed and wanted to run you'd normally shift straight to Urshul, but because you have low Harmony, you are forced to go through all of the forms in-between, one turn at a time, before you can do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T15:02:11-07:00","id":463916,"title":"","content":"No, see that doesn't square up with the preceding paragraph, which is about <i>resisting</i> the shift. It wouldn't make sense for someone to have difficulty not shifting most of the time to suddenly have to drag it out when they're stressed. That's pretty much the exact opposite of the problem they're supposed to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T15:15:36-07:00","id":463923,"title":"","content":"Not really though. They have to shift more times that would otherwise be necessary to get to the form they want. That's exactly the problem they're supposed to have, that they shift too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T15:26:24-07:00","id":463928,"title":"","content":"But what we;re describing <i>isn't</i> shifting too much. It's shifting too <i>little</i>. You can't have someone who is supposed to be all fluid suddenly start creaking between forms like a rusty Transformer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T15:31:05-07:00","id":463943,"title":"","content":"They're not supposed to be fluid, their harmony is out of whack. They literally can't help shifting more than they need to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T20:07:21-07:00","id":464217,"title":"","content":"I just took for granted that you only got to shape shift once per turn, so the force shift was what you got instead of what you wanted, unless you roll with it.Lets try an example:<br /> <br /> Say I'm a Harmony 3 werewolf chill'in in the bar minding my own beeswax, in Hishu of course, when a scmuck walks up to me and just pulls a knife! Now, because I have low harmony, my instincts are driving me toward Garou, 'cuz that's for fight'in, but I don't want to hit them with full lunacy, so I just allow my crappy harmony shape shifting to take me to Dalu, and I take a swing at him. Next turn, my body still wants full Garou, I disagree given the situation, so I spend a point of essence to prevent myself from shifting, because my body is attempting to make shape shifts, and I'm consciously fighting it, I can't make any other shape shifting this turn either. So I punch him again and put him down.<br /> <br /> Had I been Harmony 1, then I would be in a really nasty bind on that second turn, because I would have to both spend 1 point of essence, and a simple action just to prevent myself from progressing toward Garou. I could use my movement to try to get away from the assailant, but given that he's a wacko with a knife, he's probably pretty determined, without some other help, I've gotta go full Garou and put him in the dirt. Afterwards, there's no more threat, and I probably want to lay low, which desires Hishu, I decide to roll with it and go back to full human and see if I can't blend in with the crowd to avoid the cops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T20:43:22-07:00","id":464238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wild-Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462553-low-harmony?p=464217#post464217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just took for granted that you only got to shape shift once per turn, so the force shift was what you got instead of what you wanted, unless you roll with it.Lets try an example:<br /> <br /> Say I'm a Harmony 3 werewolf chill'in in the bar minding my own beeswax, in Hishu of course, when a scmuck walks up to me and just pulls a knife! Now, because I have low harmony, my instincts are driving me toward Garou, 'cuz that's for fight'in, but I don't want to hit them with full lunacy, so I just allow my crappy harmony shape shifting to take me to Dalu, and I take a swing at him. Next turn, my body still wants full Garou, I disagree given the situation, so I spend a point of essence to prevent myself from shifting, because my body is attempting to make shape shifts, and I'm consciously fighting it, I can't make any other shape shifting this turn either. So I punch him again and put him down.<br /> <br /> Had I been Harmony 1, then I would be in a really nasty bind on that second turn, because I would have to both spend 1 point of essence, and a simple action just to prevent myself from progressing toward Garou. I could use my movement to try to get away from the assailant, but given that he's a wacko with a knife, he's probably pretty determined, without some other help, I've gotta go full Garou and put him in the dirt. Afterwards, there's no more threat, and I probably want to lay low, which desires Hishu, I decide to roll with it and go back to full human and see if I can't blend in with the crowd to avoid the cops.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I thought at first, but it says you can't spend essence to resist the forced shift in stressful situations like combat. It's only the obligatory once per scene shift that you get to resist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T03:17:00-07:00","id":464484,"title":"","content":"That's at odds with the shifting chart itself though, which says that at harmony 2-3 you can either use an instant action or spend essence reflexively. Why would you need to resist reflexively <i>except</i> in combat? <br /> <br /> Actually reading it again I get the feeling that passage only refers to uratha right at the bottom of the scale. Although I'd still have them go straight into whatever they need because if your body and you want to get somewhere fast and you end up spending a turn in your second-slowest form that benefits nobody. <br /> <br /> Like, your suggesting that a character's instincts go &quot;Run! be a wolf!&quot; and the character goes &quot;Yes! Be a wolf!&quot; and then they end up in dalu and the thing chasing them catches up because they <i>really </i>needed the speed. Just, no. That's not an issue they should be facing at that point. <i>High</i> harmony werewolves can't reach the form they need. <i>Low</i> harmony werewolves get the form they need <i>whether they want to or not</i>. Sometimes becoming a wolf is inconvenient. Like when you're surrounded by normal humans. Or need hands to carry something. <i>That's</i> when the drawback rears it's head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T08:24:28-07:00","id":464698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462553-low-harmony?p=464484#post464484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's at odds with the shifting chart itself though, which says that at harmony 2-3 you can either use an instant action or spend essence reflexively. Why would you need to resist reflexively <i>except</i> in combat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beats me, but that's what the text says.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462553-low-harmony?p=464484#post464484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually reading it again I get the feeling that passage only refers to uratha right at the bottom of the scale. Although I'd still have them go straight into whatever they need because if your body and you want to get somewhere fast and you end up spending a turn in your second-slowest form that benefits nobody.</div> </div> </div> </div>What part makes you think it's only referring to Harmony 0-1 characters?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462553-low-harmony?p=464484#post464484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, your suggesting that a character's instincts go &quot;Run! be a wolf!&quot; and the character goes &quot;Yes! Be a wolf!&quot; and then they end up in dalu and the thing chasing them catches up because they <i>really </i>needed the speed. Just, no. That's not an issue they should be facing at that point. <i>High</i> harmony werewolves can't reach the form they need. <i>Low</i> harmony werewolves get the form they need <i>whether they want to or not</i>. Sometimes becoming a wolf is inconvenient. Like when you're surrounded by normal humans. Or need hands to carry something. <i>That's</i> when the drawback rears it's head.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that seems like the intent, but the actual rules just don't seem to support that. They explicitly shift one form per turn towards an appropriate form. They explicitly cannot spend essence or an action to resist the shift. But as you pointed out, if they could still shift as a reflexive action at-will, the drawback wouldn't really do much, since they'd either shift straight to the goal form if they wanted it, or immediately shift back if they didn't. I mean, I guess shifting back and forth like that might be inappropriate in some situations as well, but I don't think the intent is that you should be able to just go back and forth between Hushu and Dalu until the fight is over.<br /> <br /> The only way to reconcile this without ignoring portions of the text, like the part that says you shift one form towards an appropriate goal form per turn, and the part that says you can't resist the shift under stress, is if that's the only shifting you can do under stress at all. I agree that it seems a little strange narratively. Maybe your protean body panics and fumbles to get to the form it wants? I don't know, but I can't see any other interpretation that both complies with the rules as written and makes sense from a mechanical perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-01-2015, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T10:34:08-07:00","id":464844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462553-low-harmony?p=464698#post464698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beats me, but that's what the text says.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My whole point is that the text doesn't make any damn sense. It only talks about not being able to <i>resist</i> the change. Why would <i>not</i> resisting get you anywhere but the form you actually wanted to be in? It just does. not. work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T12:29:47-07:00","id":464966,"title":"","content":"The whole context of the &quot;shifts one form towards an appropriate form each turn&quot; bit is resisting the change. The person can spend Essence each scene to keep in one form for longer, unless [enter paragraph in question].<br /> My point here is that it seems like &quot;one form towards&quot; is the extent of the resistance the low-Harmony Uratha is able to put up, if they want to resist the change at all. In the &quot;Run! be a wolf! / Yes! be a wolf!&quot; scenario, they're not trying to resist the change and they can get right to it.<br /> If their instincts go &quot;Run! Be a wolf!&quot; and their brain is more like &quot;But this box I'm holding is important!!!!&quot; then they've got to shift, but maybe they can spend the next turn in Dalu and put the box down. Then on the next turn it can be Urhan.<br /> <br /> I said this bit about the forms before, but it seems to have been overlooked or something. As much as the five forms make a neat line on the character sheet, there's not actually an order to them. Most-like-a-regular-human to most-like-a-normal-wolf they go in the Hishu, Dalu, Gauru, Urshul, Urhan line-up. Biggest to smallest they're Gauru, Urshul, Dalu, Hishu, Urhan. Highest Speed stat to lowest they're Urshul, Urhan, Gauru, Dalu, Hishu. Most obviously out of place in a bar to least they go Gauru, Urshul, Urhan, Dalu, Hishu.<br /> Where you're shifting from and where you're shifting to both matter. So does your willingness to get there and your ability to convince the ST that the form you do take is &quot;towards&quot; what you should probably be doing.<br /> <br /> That all said, if your Harmony is 3 or lower, what you should really be doing is eating a cheeseburger to get your Harmony back on straight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T12:39:06-07:00","id":464976,"title":"","content":"Initially I was a little disappointed with this thread, because it felt like I was frustrated about something that everyone else wasn't having issues with. I couldn't grok how the system was supposed to work.<br /> <br /> Now, however, I think we've delved into it enough to realize that the Low Harmony stuff <b>really</b> needs a bit of clarification. I totally love Charlaquin's interpretation, by the way, but it doesn't totally mesh if you're willing to change directly to the form you need.<br /> <br /> All in all, I think L5 sums it up best:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462553-low-harmony?p=464844#post464844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My whole point is that the text doesn't make any damn sense. It only talks about not being able to <i>resist</i> the change. Why would <i>not</i> resisting get you anywhere but the form you actually wanted to be in? It just does. not. work.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T13:33:30-07:00","id":465097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462553-low-harmony?p=464844#post464844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My whole point is that the text doesn't make any damn sense. It only talks about not being able to <i>resist</i> the change. Why would <i>not</i> resisting get you anywhere but the form you actually wanted to be in? It just does. not. work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, it needs clarification. I'm just trying to divine the writers' intent. I think Terra Ben has it right - if you do want to shift into the goal form, you just do. If you don't want to take that form, you can slow the process by shifting one form closer to it each turn. It would be nice to know what &quot;order&quot; the forms go in, or if that's supposed to depend on the situation and ST discretion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}